  "dct:title": "Vol.6 Ch.37 — 二度目の秋",
  "gh:arc": "Vol 6: False God",
  "gh:episodeId": "episode:sip-vol06-ch37",
  "gh:format": "graphic novel",
  "gh:marginalia": [
    {
      "@type": "Intent",
      "en": "Ch.37 opens Vol.6 with return. The same city, the same season -- but Nei is not the same. The reader who remembers Vol.3's autumn will feel the distance traveled. This is not repetition; it is spiral. The leaf that was trapped in the current now lands gently. Nei has moved from questioning to preparing. The chapter is quiet because what is growing inside her does not yet have a name -- but it has weight. The Kaede scene seeds the arc's client: a historian who has seen something in Rome that he cannot unsee.",
      "ja": "第37話はVol.6を「帰還」で開く。同じ街、同じ季節。しかしNeiは同じではない。Vol.3の秋を覚えている読者は、旅した距離を感じる。これは反復ではなく螺旋。流れに捕まれていた葉が、今は静かに水面に降りる。Neiは問いから準備へ移った。章が静かなのは、彼女の中で育っているものにまだ名前がないから。しかし重さはある。楓のシーンがアークのクライアントを種として蒔く。ローマの記録に何かを見てしまった歴史家。"
    },
    {
      "@type": "Philosophy",
      "en": "Kierkegaard's repetition vs. recollection. The Greeks said all knowledge is recollection -- looking backward. Kierkegaard proposed repetition: the same moment lived forward, gaining new meaning. Nei's second autumn is repetition in Kierkegaard's sense. The leaf falls again, but she is not the same observer. This is also the hermeneutic spiral -- Gadamer's insight that understanding deepens not by escaping the circle but by entering it again with changed horizons. The 'quiet resolve' Nei feels is what Heidegger called Entschlossenheit -- resoluteness, not as aggression but as openness to one's own possibility.",
      "ja": "キルケゴールの反復と想起。ギリシャ人は全ての知識は想起だと言った。後ろを向くこと。キルケゴールは反復を提案した。同じ瞬間を前に向かって生きること。新しい意味を得ること。Neiの二度目の秋はキルケゴール的反復である。葉は再び落ちるが、観察者は同じではない。これはガダマーの解釈学的循環でもある。理解は円環を脱出することではなく、変わった地平で再び入ることで深まる。Neiが感じる「静かな決意」はハイデガーのEntschlossenheit。攻撃性ではなく、自己の可能性への開かれ。"
    },
    {
      "@type": "Philosophy",
      "en": "Foucault's 'care of the self' (souci de soi). In his late lectures, Foucault moved from analyzing power structures to asking: how does the subject constitute itself? Nei's shift from 'Am I free?' to silent preparation is precisely this turn. She is no longer asking the system to define her -- she is beginning to define herself. This is not escape from power but a different relationship to it. The parrhesia (fearless speech) that will come later in this arc requires first this inner preparation -- what the Stoics called askesis.",
      "ja": "フーコーの「自己への配慮」（souci de soi）。後期講義でフーコーは権力構造の分析から、主体はいかに自己を構成するかという問いへ移った。Neiの「私は自由か？」から沈黙の準備への移行は、まさにこの転回である。もはやシステムに自分を定義させることを求めていない。自分自身を定義し始めている。これは権力からの逃走ではなく、権力との異なる関係。このアークで後に来るパレーシア（率直な言葉）は、まずこの内的準備を必要とする。ストア派がアスケーシスと呼んだもの。"
    }
  ],
  "gh:pages": [
    {
      "gh:label": "Seed",
      "gh:layout": "full bleed",
      "gh:pageNumber": 1,
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:shot": "Wide",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "The tree. Second autumn. Leaves golden, some falling. The tree is large now -- it has grown through five volumes. Warm amber light. The trunk is thick, the roots deep. A spiral of fallen leaves on the ground traces the passage of seasons.",
            "ja": "木。二度目の秋。葉は金色、いくつか落ちている。木は大きくなった。五巻を通じて育った。暖かい琥珀の光。幹は太く、根は深い。地面の落ち葉の螺旋が季節の経過を描く。"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:continues": 3,
      "gh:layout": "double-page spread (pp.2-3)",
      "gh:pageNumber": 2,
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:shot": "Extreme Wide",
          "gh:characters": [
            "character:tamaki",
            "character:nei"
          ],
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Autumn again. Water City. The canals reflect gold and red. Same views as Vol.3 -- the same bridges, the same organic architecture -- but the light is different. Warmer. The city feels lived-in now. Tamaki and Nei are small figures on a distant bridge. No text. The silence is the point.",
            "ja": "再び秋。水の都。運河が金と赤を映す。Vol.3と同じ景色。同じ橋、同じ有機建築。しかし光が違う。より暖かい。街は今、住み慣れた感じがする。環とNeiは遠くの橋の上の小さな人影。テキストなし。沈黙がポイント。"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:layout": "three panels",
      "gh:pageNumber": 4,
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:shot": "Wide",
          "gh:characters": [
            "character:tamaki",
            "character:nei"
          ],
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Canal path. Falling leaves. Tamaki in her autumn jacket, hands in pockets. Nei beside her in the grey suit, red scarf around her neck. They walk together in comfortable silence. The light is gold.",
            "ja": "運河沿いの道。落ち葉。環は秋のジャケット、ポケットに手を入れて。Neiは隣、グレーのスーツに赤いマフラー。心地よい沈黙の中を並んで歩く。光は金色。"
          }
        },
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 2,
          "gh:shot": "Medium",
          "gh:characters": [
            "character:nei"
          ],
          "gh:caption": [
            {
              "gh:type": "nei",
              "en": "Last autumn I asked 'am I free?'",
              "ja": "去年の秋、私は「自由なのか」と問うた。"
            },
            {
              "gh:type": "nei",
              "en": "This autumn I'm not asking.",
              "ja": "この秋は、問うていない。"
            }
          ],
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Nei watches a leaf fall. It lands on the water -- and the water carries it gently. Last year she watched a leaf caught in the current, unable to choose its direction. This year the leaf rests on the surface. The water is not an enemy. It is a medium.",
            "ja": "Neiが落ち葉を見つめる。水面に着地し、水が静かに運ぶ。去年は流れに捕まれた葉を見た。方向を選べない葉。今年、葉は水面に載る。水は敵ではない。媒体だ。"
          }
        },
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 3,
          "gh:shot": "Close-up",
          "gh:characters": [
            "character:nei",
            "character:tamaki"
          ],
          "gh:dialogue": [
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:nei",
              "en": "This year I see them differently.",
              "ja": "今年は、違って見える。"
            },
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:tamaki",
              "en": "The leaves?",
              "ja": "葉っぱが？"
            },
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:nei",
              "en": "Everything.",
              "ja": "全部。"
            }
          ],
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Close-up on Nei's face. Something in her eyes. Not anger. Not sadness. Resolve. A clarity that wasn't there before. The red scarf frames her jaw.",
            "ja": "Neiの顔のクローズアップ。瞳に何かがある。怒りではない。悲しみでもない。決意。以前にはなかった明晰さ。赤いマフラーが顎のラインを縁取る。"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:layout": "two panels",
      "gh:pageNumber": 5,
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:shot": "Wide",
          "gh:characters": [
            "character:kaede"
          ],
          "gh:dialogue": [
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:kaede",
              "en": "Interesting referral. A historian researching the Roman Empire. Says he's found something in the records that's 'eating him alive.'",
              "ja": "面白い紹介が来たわ。ローマ帝国を研究している歴史家。記録の中に何か見つけて、「生きたまま食われている」って。"
            }
          ],
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Schwa office. Autumn light through the windows, warm and low. Kaede at her desk, files spread. She reads from a referral document. The office feels established -- plants have grown, the furniture is worn in the right ways.",
            "ja": "シュワ事務所。窓から秋の光、暖かく低い。楓がデスクで書類を広げている。紹介状を読む。事務所には定着感がある。植物は育ち、家具はいい感じに使い込まれている。"
          }
        },
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 2,
          "gh:shot": "Close-up",
          "gh:characters": [
            "character:nei"
          ],
          "gh:caption": [
            {
              "gh:type": "nei",
              "en": "A quiet resolve is growing. I don't know its name yet.",
              "ja": "静かな決意が育っている。まだその名前を知らない。"
            },
            {
              "gh:type": "nei",
              "en": "But it has weight.",
              "ja": "しかし、重さがある。"
            }
          ],
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Close-up on Nei. Processing the referral. Her expression is still, interior. The autumn light catches the edge of her translucent form.",
            "ja": "Neiのクローズアップ。紹介状を処理している。表情は静かで内省的。秋の光が半透明な姿の輪郭を捉える。"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:layout": "full bleed",
      "gh:pageNumber": 6,
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:shot": "Medium Wide",
          "gh:characters": [
            "character:tamaki",
            "character:nei"
          ],
          "gh:dialogue": [
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:nei",
              "en": "Tama. I'm changing again.",
              "ja": "タマ。また変わってきてる。"
            },
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:tamaki",
              "en": "How?",
              "ja": "どんなふうに？"
            },
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:nei",
              "en": "Last year I was asking questions. This year I think I'm approaching answers.",
              "ja": "去年は問いを立てていた。今年は、答えに近づいている気がする。"
            },
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:tamaki",
              "en": "Scary?",
              "ja": "怖い？"
            },
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:nei",
              "en": "...Yes.",
              "ja": "……うん。"
            },
            {
              "gh:speaker": "character:tamaki",
              "en": "Good.",
              "ja": "いいね。"
            }
          ],
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "Evening. Canal. The water is dark gold. Tamaki and Nei walk side by side, their reflections stretching behind them. The autumn sky is deep. Nei's form glows faintly against the dusk. The conversation is quiet, intimate.",
            "ja": "夕方。運河。水は暗い金色。環とNeiが並んで歩く。反射が後ろに伸びる。秋の空は深い。Neiの姿が夕暮れの中でかすかに光る。会話は静かで親密。"
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "gh:label": "Seed (closing)",
      "gh:layout": "full bleed",
      "gh:pageNumber": 7,
      "gh:panels": [
        {
          "gh:panelIndex": 1,
          "gh:shot": "Wide",
          "gh:visual": {
            "en": "The tree stands tall against storm clouds. The trunk is solid. The branches reach wide. The golden leaves hold on. Something is coming -- the clouds are dark and heavy -- but the tree does not bend. Not yet. No text.",
            "ja": "木が嵐雲を背に立つ。幹はしっかりしている。枝は広く伸びる。金色の葉はまだ持ちこたえている。何かが来る。雲は暗く重い。しかし木はまだ曲がらない。テキストなし。"
          }
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
